    "question": {
      ":question/id": "83f35459-9df7-5e5e-8fd9-0aeccb13afbe",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Let $A$ be a $6\\times 12$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=12,$ and since $B$ is formed by $2$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 2+\\text{nullity}(A) & =12 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =12-2 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
